{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966811,"nonce":"WiGSkbYPKd6opeB7C7fmyyJ3vic=","title":"Class-based CSS rules don't apply consistently — animations don't start, clip-path makes","message":"CSS overrides are inconsistent across the layer-application pipeline. Users have flagged this in reports. Concrete gaps found while attempting a CSS-driven spinner rewrite in May 2026:\n\n1. **Class-based `@keyframes` animations don't start.** `RenderTree::start_all_css_animations` (`crates/blinc_layout/src/renderer/animation/css.rs:202`) iterates `ElementRegistry::all_ids()` — that map is populated by `.id(...)` calls only. A div styled by `.class(\"foo\")` with a matching `.foo { animation: ... }` rule never gets the animation registered. styling_demo's animated elements all use `#id` selectors, which is why they work; class-based animation has no test coverage.\n\n2. **Class-based `clip-path: polygon(...)` clips the element to nothing.** Same polygon applied through `Div::clip_path(...)` (inline) renders fine; same polygon applied through a class selector silently culls the element entirely (no border, no background, nothing). Either the polygon vertices aren't propagating through the class-style apply path or the apply happens before bounds are known.\n\n3. **Class selectors leak across components.** Adding a `.cn-spinner__arc { clip-path: ...; background: ... }` rule caused a small magenta-blue artifact to appear inside switch knobs (which use `.cn-switch-thumb` / `.cn-switch-track`). The class names share no whole word. Suspect: CSS parser handles `__` weirdly OR class index matches by substring.\n\n**Why:** The CSS parser, stylesheet selector matching, animation start, and clip-path resolution were each built incrementally and tested primarily with ID-based selectors (`styling_demo` proves the ID path). The class-selector path has multiple unreviewed pinch points.\n\n**How to apply:** Any work that needs CSS to behave consistently across class and ID selectors will hit one or more of these. Until fixed, the safe paths are:\n- Inline programmatic styling via `Div::bg / .border / .clip_path / ...` for static props\n- ID-based CSS for animations and complex selectors\n- `style!` / `css!` scoped macros that produce `ElementStyle` applied inline\n\nAvoid class-only CSS for: animations, clip-path, anything that doesn't show up in style_demo's class section.\n\nSee `crates/blinc_layout/src/css_parser.rs::index_class_styles`,\n`crates/blinc_layout/src/renderer/animation/css.rs::start_all_css_animations`,\nand the class-vs-id branches in `crates/blinc_layout/src/renderer/stylesheet/base.rs`.","files":null}]}